{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,-2y-1\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+2z}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-2y-1,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={y}^{2}+2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=0+\\pi =\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\pi "] ["math" "{sin}^{2}⁡z+\\pi -8"] ["math" "{sin}^{2}⁡z-8"] ["math" "{y}^{2}+2z-2y"] ["math" "{y}^{2}+2z-2y-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le z\\le 8,\\,0\\le x\\le {z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={z}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le z\\le 8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2y}^{8}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dz\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2y}^{8}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=2y+8.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2y+3"] ["math" "2y+8"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2y+8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,-3\\le x\\le 5{y}^{4}+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-3\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=5{y}^{4}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dz"] ["math" "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA"] ["math" "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA"] ["math" "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5,\\,-\\sqrt{y+z}\\le x\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-\\sqrt{y+z},\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=4+5=9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "1-z"] ["math" "4+\\sqrt{y+z}"] ["math" "4-\\sqrt{y+z}"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161545" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,yz\\le x\\le 4},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161545" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=yz\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161545" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161545" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161545" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{yz}^{4}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{yz}^{4}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dy"] ["math" "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA"] ["math" "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA"] ["math" "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161545" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}12z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-{y}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}12z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}12z[x]_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12z(y-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{y}^{2}}12yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=4-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6y(4-{y}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(96y-48{y}^{3}+6{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[48{y}^{2}-12{y}^{4}+{y}^{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =48(2)^{2}-12(2)^{4}+(2)^{6} \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-40395" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40395" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "64"] ["math" "72"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40395" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "64"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2y}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}2[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+2z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2(y+2z-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[2yz+2{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2y(2y)+2(2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}4{y}^{2}+8{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}12{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[4{y}^{3}]_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =4(27-1) \\\\  & =104\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "104"] ["math" "124"] ["math" "76"] ["math" "82"] ["math" "94"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "104"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{4-2y}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}[2z{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2z({z}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2y}}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{4-2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{4-2y)})^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(4-2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(16-16y+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8-8y+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8y-4{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =16-16+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161561" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161561" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{22}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161561" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{16}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2z}}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,y\\le z\\le y+1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2z}}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{4}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{2z}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{4}(2z-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{2}z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{2}z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{y}^{y+1}\\frac{1}{2}z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}[{z}^{2}]_{z=y}^{z=y+1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}((y+1)^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}(2y+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[{y}^{2}+y]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(9+3)-\\frac{1}{4}(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161571" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161571" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161571" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le y}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}2[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({(\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}})}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2{y}^{2}z+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(81-0) \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "26"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "54"] ["math" "68"] ["math" "90"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "54"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2+2{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,-z\\le x\\le 0}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2+2{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-z}^{0}2+2{e}^{x}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-z}^{0}2+2{e}^{x}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-z}^{0}2+2{e}^{x}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[2x+2{e}^{x}]_{x=-z}^{x=0}dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}0+2{e}^{0}-2(-z)-2{e}^{-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2+2z-2{e}^{-z}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2+2z-2{e}^{-z}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}2+2z-2{e}^{-z}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[2z+{z}^{2}+2{e}^{-z}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(2+1+2{e}^{-1})-2{e}^{0}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}1+2{e}^{-1}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}1+2{e}^{-1}\\,dy & =(1+2{e}^{-1})[y]_{y=-1}^{y=0} \\\\  & =(1+2{e}^{-1})(0-(-1)) \\\\  & =2{e}^{-1}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{-1}+1"] ["math" "3-{e}^{2}"] ["math" "3{e}^{-1}-2"] ["math" "4{e}^{2}-1"] ["math" "8-3e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{e}^{-1}+1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z=-{y}^{2}$ in the fourth quadrant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[x]_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/38ea49a6fae41574107b2ba68a578586a306cf43d419d4de5699dcfa009137c2.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[({y}^{2}+1)z+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=-{y}^{2}}^{z=0}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1)((0-(-{y}^{2}))+\\frac{1}{3}(0-{(-{y}^{2})}^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1){y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{21}{y}^{7}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{105}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{34}{81}"] ["math" "\\frac{61}{105}"] ["math" "\\frac{67}{92}"] ["math" "\\frac{72}{121}"] ["math" "\\frac{79}{100}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{61}{105}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le z\\sqrt{3}},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axes, the line $y=2$ and the line $z=y$ in the first quadrant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z\\sqrt{3}}2y\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z\\sqrt{3}}2y\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}2y[x]_{x=0}^{x=z\\sqrt{3}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/63a8768b2769fad339ba7667357812d2dda0ea856e846ad666a100f8bc1336e9.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}2z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{16}{4}-0) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-40208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le y+z+2},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the $z$-axis and the line $z=2-y$ in the first quadrant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z+2}y\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z+2}y\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}y[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+z+2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y(y+z+2)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/b473cc75dbbd6fa36ba43f6bbdec4a0133164e6fd8bc5f76ff86cec74714a256.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[({y}^{2}+2y)z+\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2-y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}+2y)(2-y)+\\frac{1}{2}y(2-y)^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4y-{y}^{3})+\\frac{1}{2}y(4-4y+{y}^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}-2{y}^{2}+6y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{4}-\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}+3{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =-2-\\frac{16}{3}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le yz},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z={y}^{2}$ in the first quadrant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(yz)^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/acb173db9d28ed8b38e63c7bc365c20e5755aeb1af3f6340e7b9229a4b49101d.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z={y}^{2}}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}({y}^{6}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{8}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{9}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{9}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{18}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{27}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/ca49b92d602d04a73dc7ab9936d601654bd293ce3fb7950372ac86155875aca3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/0008ba406cfe8a5b61d683a6854260897cb441752a5333add281ab1279e31b0b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/bbe6b6b897e5d53421080ae8e8b9dc49f2ea1b7e135f8426ee3f11af01cc2401.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}(2-\\frac{y}{3}+z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(3)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy & =[y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161784" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161784" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161784" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/3fe3ec24f8f8006f22bde8ba2dc39fd3cd3f73668b06f8ea4a74e4ed5206a193.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/2a20f2651c24e48871028b44fe61da4600d632481877ef32ccdfd3241262a53b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/1ba7c02f254313a73a813e4e43c44c25523ce77dd47e594a1db3b412a6bd5c3d.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=5-y-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}(5-y-\\frac{z}{2})\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{z}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=4}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy & =[2y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =6-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/d5690bff5819d72cc9d49016c119dc79f62f4d766c142a43a89df196ce9f2335.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/2427e053c0e2d808b32db5d7fedf81365e7e50f0b3f2dc61598ad1795394686e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+2y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2+2y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{y}^{2}z+2{y}^{3}z-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/bc1b0ea463b0f753a2c65784fa5d46203cde8f457116c481301bf3f20ce82f54.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4y\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/9bb9311cbaf796f76c4b8b7cb7ed81abec48abc445b894f838f940fbd92e534b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/82f237dc5fb7d8b8ed34b7a1c16527ab338923a33462f0bd7dafbe54bc5e5158.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y-z}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4y\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}4y\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}4y\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}4y\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4y[x]_{x=0}^{x=4-y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4y(4-y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(16y-4{y}^{2}-4yz)\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(16y-4{y}^{2}-4yz)\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(16y-4{y}^{2}-4yz)\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[16yz-4{y}^{2}z-2y{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(14y-4{y}^{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(14y-4{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={[7{y}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(28-\\frac{32}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-40219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "\\frac{40}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{52}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-40219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{52}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/f1f3493cd1ff0bee115bf7c311504a2b8a9bbd38dd35adae96c9f7abcae40ae1.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type II region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/6cc327f63d7141c43852e868812a7cff1ec9ae0acfed636ff896ceb204b6fbf0.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\n(y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2}=1\\,⟺\\,z=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a0fb19d32c2545e5c2a61cbb54536e7c28b1a54dbce51c7752c3687035d6c3d6.png)\n\nHence, $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}[{x}^{2}]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2fa4e9cfbf5cd391c9a944b3f1daf13566214d3e28e62d54960fdca809c7c7b7"} {"question" "q-161594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}3z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "q-161594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/state.json" "file_sha256" "cba82612441407fa8b14581778bd70062ef470ef8aed266d6df563b576f4dfa8"} {"question" "e-12398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V\n= \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \nf(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region defined as\n\n$$\nR=\\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -y^2 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{y}, \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq ye^{z+2} \\right\\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-12398.json" "file_sha256" "8da20a91a5c4b22474fdd0e48a9fffa83253af104be64b9e37d1bed07cbf17f1"} {"question" "e-12398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z)  \\: : \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\: u_1(y,z) \\leq x \\leq u_2(y,z) \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm d V = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[\\int_{u_1(y,z)}^{u_2(y,z)} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm{d}x \\right]\\,\\textrm d A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu_1(y,z) = -2, \\qquad u_2(y,z)  = ye^{z+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{-2}^{ye^{z+2}} f(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\right] \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD =\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -y^2 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2}^{y{e}^{z+2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}[{\\int }_{-2}^{y{e}^{z+2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dz\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}{\\int }_{-2}^{y{e}^{z+2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-12398.json" "file_sha256" "8da20a91a5c4b22474fdd0e48a9fffa83253af104be64b9e37d1bed07cbf17f1"} {"question" "e-11349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D \\left[ \\int_{0}^{z} \\dfrac{\\cos (2y)}{1-y} \\,\\textrm{d}x \\right] \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (y,z) \\, : \\, 0 \\leq y \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 2\\sqrt{1-y} \\right\\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-11349.json" "file_sha256" "5cadbca05236b713ec2cc5055d9c0fc32ac3eee3ce8ddd3d4cc2a3c4f2c115a5"} {"question" "e-11349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}[x]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}(z-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\sqrt{1-y}}\\frac{z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}{[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2\\sqrt{1-y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}(\\frac{4(1-y)}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-11349.json" "file_sha256" "5cadbca05236b713ec2cc5055d9c0fc32ac3eee3ce8ddd3d4cc2a3c4f2c115a5"} {"question" "e-11348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 4x^3  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\right\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the $z$-axis, and the line $z = 4-y$ in the first quadrant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-11348.json" "file_sha256" "fc1c9b79fb3f130f1d97658d3604425ff98108e27da250778a9aab1f065a4f26"} {"question" "e-11348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} 4x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}V\n= \n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}} 4x^3 \\, \\mathrm{d}x \\right] \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}4{x}^{3}\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{4}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{(\\sqrt{y})}^{4}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/3c8712fa0a30ad94f503efe5e080ee89f83eb21f19fba45033bbedeab08ac816.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y}{y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y}{y}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{y}^{2}z]_{z=0}^{z=4-y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{y}^{2}(4-y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}4{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(64-0)-\\frac{1}{4}(256-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-11348.json" "file_sha256" "fc1c9b79fb3f130f1d97658d3604425ff98108e27da250778a9aab1f065a4f26"} {"question" "e-12369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/fc19dd4415663ab027e0fc386d4c5bc81a28c1bc26d5f6cf2083f4f4228a4dea.png)\n\n \n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 12z^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-12369.json" "file_sha256" "f7772168d0b6688c0508d83f82735f6bad36685d6575781195e79cb065ddb9f9"} {"question" "e-12369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/f25c393f10c35ffd9b4fa91cdf672a516cf6cff974a8aa563d350619a64b79bd.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y-z \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y-z \\big\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\iiint \\limits_{R}  12z^2  \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{3-y-z}  12z^2  \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3-y-z}12{z}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-y-z}12{z}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}12{z}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=3-y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}12{z}^{2}(3-y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{z}^{2}-12y{z}^{2}-12{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{z}^{2}-12y{z}^{2}-12{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{z}^{2}-12y{z}^{2}-12{z}^{3})\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[12{z}^{3}-4y{z}^{3}-3{z}^{4}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(12-4y-3)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9-4y)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9-4y)\\,dy & =[9y-2{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(9-2)-0 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/example-12369.json" "file_sha256" "f7772168d0b6688c0508d83f82735f6bad36685d6575781195e79cb065ddb9f9"}] "usage" {"q-40208" [] "e-11349" [] "e-12398" [] "q-40395" [] "e-12369" [] "q-40219" [] "e-11348" []} "basis" 2048 "retractions" [[17592186134210 :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$∬_(D)[∫_{0}^{y}12zdx]dA$\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n$D = {(y, z): 0 \\le y \\le 2, 0 \\le z \\le 4 - y^{2}}$."] [17592186134193 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)2ydV$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n$R = {(x, y, z): (y, z) ∈ D, 0 \\le x \\le z\\sqrt{3}}$,\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axes, the line $y = 2$ and the line $z = y$ in the first quadrant."] [17592186134196 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2141/Source/Images/q-40219.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral\n$∭_(R)4ydV$\nover the region $R$, shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*"] [17592186133405 :question/problem "Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below\n\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V = \\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} f(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region defined as\n\n$R=\\left\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -y^2 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{y}, \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq ye^{z+2} \\right\\}$."] [17592186133405 :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\: u_1(y,z) \\leq x \\leq u_2(y,z) \\big\\}\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2141/Source/Images/83d78c3a80d9921c38438e2967052d69.png)\n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm d V = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[\\int_{u_1(y,z)}^{u_2(y,z)} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm{d}x \\right]\\,\\textrm d A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu_1(y,z) = -2, \\qquad u_2(y,z) = ye^{z+2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{-2}^{ye^{z+2}} f(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\right] \\mathrm{d}A\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD =\\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -y^2 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\right\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)[∫_{-2}^{ye^{z + 2}}f(x, y, z)dx]dA &= ∫_{1}^{4}∫_{-y^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}[∫_{-2}^{ye^{z + 2}}f(x, y, z)dx]dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{4}∫_{-y^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}∫_{-2}^{ye^{z + 2}}f(x, y, z)dxdzdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133397 :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D \\left[\\int_{0}^{z} \\dfrac{\\cos (2y)}{1-y} \\,\\textrm{d}x \\right] \\textrm{d}A$\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n$D = \\left\\{(y,z) \\,: \\, 0 \\leq y \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 2\\sqrt{1-y} \\right\\}$."] [17592186133397 :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)[∫_{0}^{z}(\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)dx]dA &= ∬_(D)(\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)[x]_{x = 0}^{x = z}dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)(\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)(z - 0)dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)(z\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)dA\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)(z\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)dA &= ∫_{0}^{π/6}∫_{0}^{2\\sqrt{1 - y}}(z\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π/6}(\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)[\\frac{z^{2}}{2}]_{z = 0}^{z = 2\\sqrt{1 - y}}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π/6}(\\cos (2y))/(1 - y)((4(1 - y))/(2) - 0)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π/6}2\\cos (2y)dy \\\\\n&= [\\sin (2y)]_{y = 0}^{y = π/6} \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{3}) - \\sin (0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133396 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 4x^3 \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n$R = \\left\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\right\\}$,\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the $z$-axis, and the line $z = 4-y$ in the first quadrant."] [17592186133396 :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} 4x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}V = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}} 4x^3 \\, \\mathrm{d}x \\right] \\mathrm{d}A\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)[∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}4x^{3}dx]dA &= ∬_(D)[x^{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = \\sqrt{y}}dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)(\\sqrt{y})^{4}dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)y^{2}dA\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2141/Source/Images/f91b4d0b9ed33b8d327459a73fe31766.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)y^{2}dA &= ∫_{0}^{4}∫_{0}^{4 - y}y^{2}dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}[∫_{0}^{4 - y}y^{2}dz]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}[y^{2}z]_{z = 0}^{z = 4 - y}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}y^{2}(4 - y)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}4y^{2} - y^{3}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{4}{3}y^{3} - \\frac{1}{4}y^{4}]_{y = 0}^{y = 4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3}(64 - 0) - \\frac{1}{4}(256 - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{64}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133403 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 12z^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the region $R$, shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2141/Source/Images/e1e0a37a01b5ecf240851daf1ff21f56.png)\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*"] [17592186133403 :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2141/Source/Images/a4f8d3e95c46f652b90983ba8bfa9d97.png)\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y-z \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2141/Source/Images/5b209d6360c4381ea8e24a7a857c8cba.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y-z \\big\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\iiint \\limits_{R} 12z^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V = \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{3-y-z} 12z^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{3 - y - z}12z^{2}dxdzdy &= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}[∫_{0}^{3 - y - z}12z^{2}dx]dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}12z^{2}[x]_{x = 0}^{x = 3 - y - z}dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}12z^{2}(3 - y - z)dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}(36z^{2} - 12yz^{2} - 12z^{3})dzdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}(36z^{2} - 12yz^{2} - 12z^{3})dzdy &= ∫_{0}^{1}[∫_{0}^{1}(36z^{2} - 12yz^{2} - 12z^{3})dz]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[12z^{3} - 4yz^{3} - 3z^{4}]_{z = 0}^{z = 1}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}(12 - 4y - 3)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}(9 - 4y)dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}(9 - 4y)dy &= [9y - 2y^{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = 1} \\\\\n&= (9 - 2) - 0 \\\\\n&= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131601 17592186131602 17592186131603 17592186131604 17592186131605 17592186131619 17592186131620 17592186131621 17592186131622 17592186131623 17592186131703 17592186131704 17592186131705 17592186131706 17592186131707] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131600 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131600 :answer-field/id] [17592186131600 :answer-field/key] [17592186131600 :answer-field/ty